AB  - Multimodal recommendation has advanced by leveraging modalities such as text, images, and audio, yet challenges remain in effective feature fusion and modeling long-range dependencies in interaction graphs. We propose MaMoE4Rec, a framework combining Mixture-of-Experts (MoE)–based multimodal encoding with hop-aware sequential modeling. Item modalities are encoded via modality-specific self-attention and a dynamic sparse MoE, fused with item IDs, and then tokenized with user IDs into interaction sequences. We design odd–even positional encoding to distinguish heterogeneous and homogeneous relations across hops and adopt the Mamba state space model to capture global dependencies. Experiments on public datasets demonstrate that MaMoE4Rec achieves superior performance compared to baselines, validating its effectiveness in multimodal fusion and graph modeling.
