AB  - Image captioning in Vietnamese remains underexplored, with two practical obstacles: limited native datasets with multi-reference captions and the limited ability of existing models to represent spatial relationships between objects in Vietnamese contexts. This work addresses both challenges by introducing two key contributions. First, HDUCap is proposed as a large-scale Vietnamese image captioning dataset containing diverse real-world scenes, each paired with five human-written captions. Our dataset offers richer linguistic variety and better reference coverage than existing resources. Second, a spatially-aware Transformer model is presented. It integrates a positional token embedding module to represent global object locations and a learnable attention module to capture relative spatial relationships between objects more effectively. The method is evaluated under three settings: in-domain evaluation, zero-shot transfer, and mixed-data training on public Vietnamese datasets. It shows steady improvements over strong baselines, especially on higher-order n-gram and consensus metrics, and remains stable when the data distribution changes. The HDUCap dataset and the proposed model are established as a reproducible benchmark for Vietnamese captioning, supporting further research and method comparison. The source code and dataset are available at https://github.com/long-nguyen12/HDUCap.
